   "text": {
    "L1": "This poem says that together we can do more than we can do alone.",
    "L2": "One small stick will snap, but a bundle of sticks is hard to break.",
    "L3": "One raindrop is small, but many raindrops make a waterfall.",
    "L4": "So the big idea is simple: together we are stronger than alone.",
    "L5": "The words two and true are spelt differently, but their ending sounds rhyme.",
    "L6": "Open doors means finding new chances or doing hard things, not only real doors.",
    "L7": "After can, use the plain action word: we can carry, not can carries.",
    "L8": "Now show what you know: do two and true rhyme?"
   },
